WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.478
Orchard Core builds a page from shapes, and Liquid templates decide how each shape looks.

00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:10.802
This video shows how a template draws a content item, how zones place

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:15.300
content in the layout, and how to render other content items and shapes.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.696
A shape is an object that holds the data and metadata of the

00:00:23.696 --> 00:00:26.457
thing to display, and a template draws it.

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:30.196
The template can come from a module, a theme, or the admin.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:34.280
In a Liquid template, Model is the shape that the template draws.

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:37.633
A content item becomes a Content shape.

00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:43.418
The default template of the Contents module draws its Header, Meta, Content, and Footer zones.

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:48.450
The Content zone of the item holds the shapes that its parts and fields generate.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.788
In Liquid, a name after Model reads a property of the shape, or

00:00:53.788 --> 00:00:56.248
the child shape with that name.

00:00:56.248 --> 00:01:03.163
So Model.Content is the Content zone, and Model.Content.MarkdownBodyPart is the shape of one part.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:06.620
The shape_render filter draws a shape as HTML.

00:01:10.819 --> 00:01:14.195
This is the home page of a site made with the Blog recipe.

00:01:14.195 --> 00:01:16.674
It is one content item, of the type Blog.

00:01:16.674 --> 00:01:20.999
The Blog Theme draws its layout and its content types with Liquid templates.

00:01:21.464 --> 00:01:25.029
At the top, the banner belongs to the Header zone of the layout.

00:01:25.029 --> 00:01:28.491
The template of the Blog type fills that zone with a zone tag,

00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:31.444
and the layout of the theme draws it above the page.

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:35.587
Under the banner, the Content zone holds the list of posts.

00:01:35.587 --> 00:01:39.446
A post in the list is the Summary display of its content item:

00:01:39.446 --> 00:01:42.339
a title, a subtitle, and the author and date.

00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:44.955
At the bottom is the Footer zone.

00:01:44.955 --> 00:01:48.649
A widget in a layer puts its content there, and the layout of

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:51.185
the theme draws that zone in its footer.

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:53.445
A post has its own template.

00:01:53.445 --> 00:01:57.332
It fills the Header zone of the layout with the title, the subtitle,

00:01:57.332 --> 00:02:00.589
and the author and date, and it draws the Markdown body.

00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:07.516
This is the template of the Blog Post type.

00:02:07.516 --> 00:02:12.246
It writes the title from Model.ContentItem into the Header zone, then draws the

00:02:12.246 --> 00:02:14.638
Markdown body part with shape_render.

00:02:14.638 --> 00:02:17.699
The template draws only the shapes that it names.

00:02:18.449 --> 00:02:22.558
The template of the Blog type draws its body part inside the header.

00:02:22.558 --> 00:02:27.445
Then shape_remove_item removes that shape and the image from the Content zone, and

00:02:27.445 --> 00:02:30.999
shape_render draws what remains, so nothing appears twice.

00:02:31.749 --> 00:02:35.371
A theme names a template after the shape it draws:

00:02:35.371 --> 00:02:39.899
Content-BlogPost.liquid draws the Detail display of a Blog Post.

00:02:39.899 --> 00:02:46.173
In the admin, under Design, Templates, the template is named Content__BlogPost instead, and

00:02:46.173 --> 00:02:49.989
it takes priority over a theme file of the same name.

00:02:54.189 --> 00:02:58.308
The zone tag renders the content between its tags, writes nothing at that

00:02:58.308 --> 00:03:01.801
place, and adds the result to the zone with the name you give

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.677
it, in the layout of the page.

00:03:03.677 --> 00:03:06.649
A position argument orders the content in the zone.

00:03:07.399 --> 00:03:09.359
The layout draws the zones.

00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:13.873
The render_section tag writes the zone you name, or nothing when it is

00:03:13.873 --> 00:03:18.208
empty, and with required set to true an empty zone raises an error.

00:03:18.208 --> 00:03:23.019
The render_body tag writes the layout's Content zone, which holds the page.

00:03:23.769 --> 00:03:28.911
The content of the page is drawn first, then the other zones, and the layout last.

00:03:28.911 --> 00:03:32.885
That is why a template in the Content zone can fill the Header

00:03:32.885 --> 00:03:35.339
zone, and the layout still draws it.

00:03:36.089 --> 00:03:38.588
A template can also choose another layout.

00:03:38.588 --> 00:03:42.076
The layout tag adds the name you give it to the alternates of

00:03:42.076 --> 00:03:46.242
the Layout shape, the names under which Orchard Core looks for a template.

00:03:46.242 --> 00:03:48.949
A template with that name then draws the page.

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:57.589
To draw another content item, build its display shape and render it.

00:03:57.589 --> 00:04:02.689
The shape_build_display filter takes a display type, and Detail is the default.

00:04:02.689 --> 00:04:06.349
In The Blog Theme, the list uses Summary for each post.

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:10.360
The Contents module adds the Content accessor.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.307
It loads the published item for a handle:

00:04:13.307 --> 00:04:19.579
alias, slug for the path of an Autoroute part, or contentitemid for a content item identifier.

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:24.909
When nothing matches, it returns nothing, and the render filters write nothing.

00:04:25.659 --> 00:04:30.059
The contentitem tag loads an item by handle and draws it with a

00:04:30.059 --> 00:04:32.100
display type, in one step.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:38.669
When you have a list of content item identifiers, the content_item_id filter loads them together.

00:04:42.869 --> 00:04:47.634
The shape_new filter creates a shape from its type, and each named argument

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:50.869
becomes a property, with its name in Pascal case.

00:04:50.869 --> 00:04:55.634
Here a DateTime shape gets the creation date of a post, and shape_stringify

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.869
turns the drawn shape into text.

00:04:58.619 --> 00:05:01.929
The shape tag creates a shape and draws it in one step.

00:05:01.929 --> 00:05:05.348
The layout of The Blog Theme draws the main menu with it:

00:05:05.348 --> 00:05:09.636
the alias argument becomes a property of the Menu shape, and with Dynamic

00:05:09.636 --> 00:05:12.729
Cache enabled the cache arguments cache the result.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.278
Tags change a shape before you draw it.

00:05:16.278 --> 00:05:23.243
They set its alternates, wrappers, classes, attributes, type, display type, position, tab, and properties.

00:05:23.243 --> 00:05:26.539
Each one takes the shape as its first argument.

00:05:27.289 --> 00:05:32.389
Here a post is built in the Summary display type, then given one more alternate.

00:05:32.389 --> 00:05:35.118
The last alternate added is tried first.

00:05:35.118 --> 00:05:38.973
If a template exists for it, it draws the post; if not, the

00:05:38.973 --> 00:05:40.989
earlier alternates are used.

00:05:42.989 --> 00:05:47.909
A Liquid template draws the shapes it receives, places content in zones, and

00:05:47.909 --> 00:05:49.949
renders other content items.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:54.269
The documentation of the Liquid module lists the filters and tags.

00:05:54.269 --> 00:05:55.829
Thanks for watching.

